# 0077 — The knowledge base is hyper-markdown

Status: doing
Related: [[wiki/hypermarkdown]], [[hmd-integration]],
[`doc/stack.hmd`](../stack.hmd),
[hypermarkdown issue 0009](https://github.com/ewiger/hypermarkdown/blob/main/doc/issues/0009-nested-vault-swept-into-the-outer-one.md)

`doc/` is a vault, but most of it was plain Markdown: the book, the reference,
the proposals, the issues, the models and the stack were outside the wikilink
graph and joined by relative `.md` links that nothing checked. Every document
becomes a card, so the knowledge base is one graph that `hmd lint` checks and
HQL reads.

## Shape

- **Two vaults.** `doc/public/` carries its own `.hmd/`, nested in `doc/`. The
  site is built by the `hypermarkdown` MkDocs plugin with that root, and each
  `.hmd` page is registered under its `.md` name, so `mkdocs.yml` and every URL
  stay as they were.
- **Folder notes.** A folder's `README.md` or `index.md` becomes `index.hmd`,
  so `[[HQL-0041]]` names the proposal.
- **Mechanical conversion.** A file is renamed and its links rewritten. A link
  within a vault becomes a wikilink with the shortest reference that resolves
  uniquely. Its fragment stays the heading slug. A link across vaults, or to a
  file that is not a card, stays a relative Markdown link. Prose is unchanged.
- **Stays Markdown.** Agent prompts (`*.prompt.md`) and everything under
  `.grem/`.

## Steps

- [x] The site builds through the plugin; `doc/public/` is a vault; the site
  root, install and examples pages are cards.
- [x] HQL's filesystem source skips a nested vault.
- [x] Dev docs: `stack.md`, `DEVELOP.md`, `models/`, `status/`, `wiki/`,
  `memory/`.
- [x] Proposals.
- [x] Issues, archive included, and `kanban.yaml`.
- [x] The book, `doc/public/learn/`.
- [ ] The reference: `hql reference` writes cards.
- [ ] Clean-up: no `.md` fallbacks in the tests, and `hmd lint` for both vaults
  in CI.

## Waits on

Two fixes in the `hypermarkdown` package, both for its next patch release:

- **Issue 0009.** `hmd lint --root doc` sweeps `doc/public/` into `doc/`. The
  site build is unaffected, since its root is `doc/public/`.
- **Issue 0010.** The MkDocs plugin registers a folder note `a/b/index.hmd` as
  the page `a/b.md`, and leaves its relative Markdown links resolving from
  `a/`. The hook `contrib/mkdocs/folder_notes.py` rebases them until then, and
  is deleted with the dependency bump.
